      "id": "you-manner-folding-model",
      "jlpt": 4,
      "target": "you-adverbial-comparison",
      "relationship": "you-predicate-vs-noun-modification",
      "prompt": "紙を、見本（みほん）のよう____折ってください。",
      "translation": "Use only に or な after the printed よう. Describe how to fold the paper, not what kind of paper it is: fold the paper as in the model.",
      "evidence": "The model specifies how to perform 折る, and the next word is the verb form 折って.",
      "explanation": "見本のように modifies the folding action. の already connects the noun 見本 to よう. な would need a noun to modify rather than directly connecting this comparison to 折ってください. Other formulations, including 見本のとおりに, can also describe following a model; they are outside this ending-only blank.",
      "answer": "you-adverbial-comparison",
      "acceptedAnswers": [
        "に"
      ],
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "you-adverbial-comparison",
          "label": "に",
          "rationale": "Connects the model comparison to the folding action."
        },
        {
          "id": "you-noun-modifier",
          "label": "な",
          "rationale": "Would directly modify a noun, but the following 折って is a verb form."
        }
      ],
      "vocabulary": {
