      "prompt": "子供でもこの案内が____ように、難しい漢字にふりがなを付けました。",
      "translation": "Use 読む (よむ, read) in its potential form ending in る or ない, without added words; ように is already printed. State the purpose: I added furigana to the difficult kanji so that even children could read this notice.",
      "evidence": "The furigana is intended to make reading possible, not prevent it.",
      "explanation": "読めるように identifies being able to read as the desired result of adding furigana. The main action is past, but the goal uses nonpast 読める, not 読めた. The sentence states a purpose rather than independently proving that every child successfully read the notice.",
      "answer": "you-enabled-goal",
      "acceptedAnswers": [
        "読める",
        "よめる"
      ],
      "options": [
